WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.527 --> 00:00:03.524
~~ [Dance]
[People Chattering]

2
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.937
Hi.

3
00:00:16.005 --> 00:00:17.737
Sounds like a good party.

4
00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:20.808
Twenty bucks.
Okay, no problem.

5
00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:23.883
I, uh, just-
I got it in here somewhere.

6
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:30.542
Oh, you know, I'm-

7
00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:33.987
I'm sorry. I guess I must have
forgotten to go to the machine.

8
00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:36.792
Yeah,
and brush your teeth.

9
00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:39.567
Lady, you don't have two cents.

10
00:00:40.542 --> 00:00:43.779
Well, I can- I can get it from-
from my friend who's inside.

11
00:00:43.853 --> 00:00:47.021
He can give it to me,
and then I'll bring it back out to you.
You don't know anybody here.

12
00:00:47.095 --> 00:00:52.098
Yes, I do. James. He's blond,
and he's really friendly,
and he's a big talker.

13
00:00:52.176 --> 00:00:54.546
I need to see him.

14
00:00:57.391 --> 00:00:59.955
Go on in.

15
00:01:01.871 --> 00:01:06.248
~~ [Continues]

16
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.954
James?

17
00:01:26.308 --> 00:01:28.040
James?

18
00:01:28.113 --> 00:01:29.777
James?
Hi.

19
00:01:29.851 --> 00:01:32.620
Do you know whereJames is?

20
00:01:32.693 --> 00:01:35.826
Oh, yeah, he's-
he's around here somewhere.

21
00:01:48.438 --> 00:01:51.537
[Echoing]
Let's go find him.

22
00:01:54.756 --> 00:01:57.388
James?
Do you know whereJames is?

23
00:01:57.464 --> 00:02:01.202
[Echoing]
Where is James?

24
00:02:01.275 --> 00:02:03.839
- James? James?
- [Voice Overlapping]

25
00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:06.890
James? James?

26
00:02:06.958 --> 00:02:09.761
- [Woman] Oh, yeah, he's-
he's around here somewhere.
- Where is he?

27
00:02:15.784 --> 00:02:19.351
Please.
I really need to find him.

28
00:02:30.693 --> 00:02:33.257
What are you doing?

29
00:02:35.073 --> 00:02:37.511
- Bitch!
- [Grunts]

30
00:02:41.424 --> 00:02:45.492
[Siren Wailing]

31
00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:49.068
[People Screaming, Shouting]

32
00:02:51.553 --> 00:02:54.220
No! She's trying to help me!

33
00:02:54.294 --> 00:02:58.169
[Screaming]
Get off her! Get off me!

34
00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.678
- [Screaming Continues]
- Settle down!

35
00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.057
Move!
[Gasps]

36
00:03:05.126 --> 00:03:07.564
Geez.
I didn't touch her.

37
00:03:07.633 --> 00:03:11.131
Great.
Now we gotta go to a hospital.

38
00:03:44.573 --> 00:03:48.744
Homeless. Admitted 24 hours ago
with a suspected drug overdose.

39
00:03:48.818 --> 00:03:51.519
Her tox screen's clean,
but she's still delusional.

40
00:03:51.593 --> 00:03:55.035
"Homeless."
Usually means crazy, no money.

41
00:03:55.103 --> 00:03:58.043
Cuddy's not gonna be-
We're a teaching hospital.

42
00:03:58.111 --> 00:04:00.549
No I D. Doesn't even
seem to know her name.

43
00:04:00.619 --> 00:04:03.559
I got called in because of
some lesions on her arm.

44
00:04:03.628 --> 00:04:07.070
Homeless always means no roof.
Leads to too much sun.
No, the lesions were noncancerous.

45
00:04:07.137 --> 00:04:10.670
But I noticed a twitch.
Her wrist.

46
00:04:14.158 --> 00:04:15.559
[Moans]
You feel that?

47
00:04:15.628 --> 00:04:18.727
Sure. I'm human.

48
00:04:18.804 --> 00:04:21.276
Make a fist around my fingers
as tight as you can.

49
00:04:21.345 --> 00:04:23.043
Squeeze.
I am.

50
00:04:26.126 --> 00:04:28.496
All right.

51
00:04:28.566 --> 00:04:30.970
Raise your arms
above your head for me.

52
00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:33.842
[Panting]

53
00:04:33.915 --> 00:04:36.912
- [Moans, Gasping]
- She's seizing.

54
00:04:36.991 --> 00:04:40.694
- Get me some Ativan.
- She doesn't wanna be discharged.
She's manipulating you.

55
00:04:43.709 --> 00:04:46.842
It's real.
Check a finger stick.

56
00:04:50.529 --> 00:04:54.974
- Blood sugar's 38.
- I need D-50 I.V. Push, stat.

57
00:04:56.146 --> 00:04:59.086
Fake low blood sugar.
Now, that's acting.

58
00:04:59.154 --> 00:05:01.091
The blood sugar was real.

59
00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.499
She's probably diabetic.
O.D.'d on her own insulin.

60
00:05:05.874 --> 00:05:08.814
Room 2032.
Do you have her effects out here?

61
00:05:08.883 --> 00:05:12.347
Look, a seizure buys her a place to sleep
while the nice doctors run their tests.

62
00:05:12.425 --> 00:05:15.558
Maybe a few free meals.

63
00:05:15.635 --> 00:05:18.473
Twenty bucks
says there's insulin in there.

64
00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:23.992
Oh! Wow.
Put this back, please.

65
00:05:24.059 --> 00:05:26.657
What about the twitch?
Her arm moved.

66
00:05:26.733 --> 00:05:29.673
Why fake a twitch?
In case the seizure was too subtle?

67
00:05:29.742 --> 00:05:32.682
The twitch could indicate a tumor,
which could indicate-

68
00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:36.021
A need to see a neurologist,
which is why you called me.

69
00:05:36.094 --> 00:05:39.763
Keep an eye on her till 2:00 p.m.
Watch her blood sugar,
give her a nice hot lunch.

70
00:05:39.838 --> 00:05:41.866
Then discharge her.

71
00:05:44.952 --> 00:05:48.485
- He's wrong.
- Foreman is wrong?

72
00:05:48.563 --> 00:05:51.503
The neurologist is wrong
about a neurological problem.

73
00:05:51.572 --> 00:05:54.512
He took one look at her
and figured it was a scam.

74
00:05:54.581 --> 00:05:56.518
So you figure
he's not being objective.

75
00:05:56.586 --> 00:06:00.255
House, the woman had a twitch.
She had a seizure.

76
00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.999
Both of which Foreman saw?
He just wanted her out the door!

77
00:06:04.074 --> 00:06:07.014
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Back up there, big fella.

78
00:06:07.083 --> 00:06:10.023
Foreman's the guy
you wanna take a swing at.

79
00:06:10.092 --> 00:06:12.029
[Sighs]

80
00:06:12.098 --> 00:06:15.733
I just want her
to get some medical attention.

81
00:06:17.312 --> 00:06:20.252
That's not even close to being true.

82
00:06:20.321 --> 00:06:22.816
It's something else.
Something personal.

83
00:06:26.071 --> 00:06:27.666
Give me the file.

84
00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.992
Looks like this'll be fun.

85
00:06:35.064 --> 00:06:38.597
The twitch could be a miniseizure,
unrelated to the diabetes.

86
00:06:38.674 --> 00:06:40.542
Brain tumor?

87
00:06:40.613 --> 00:06:42.550
Glad you could join us,
Eric.

88
00:06:42.619 --> 00:06:45.559
What's the differential
for a twitch in the wrist?

89
00:06:45.628 --> 00:06:49.297
The patient's a 30-ish Jane Doe.
I thought I just discharged her.

90
00:06:49.372 --> 00:06:51.674
Well, she's my patient.
No harm in a second opinion.

91
00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:54.685
A blow to the head?
A subdural hematoma?

92
00:06:54.754 --> 00:06:56.850
Read the file.
No evidence of cranial trauma.

93
00:06:56.927 --> 00:07:00.425
- A twitch could indicate a brain tumor.
- Or about a dozen other things!

94
00:07:00.504 --> 00:07:03.501
Come on. There's two things
homeless people are good at-

95
00:07:03.579 --> 00:07:05.744
getting sick and running scams.

96
00:07:05.819 --> 00:07:08.759
If you're so worried about it
being a brain tumor, get her an M.R.I.

97
00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:11.801
- When she's clear on that,
then you can bounce her out of here.
- Well, you've got her all figured out.

98
00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.938
- I've known a lot more
homeless people than you have.
- Yes, you've got that going for you.

99
00:07:16.015 --> 00:07:17.986
How could I have doubted
your medical opinion?

100
00:07:18.054 --> 00:07:21.291
The big question.
You're missing it, all of you.

101
00:07:21.364 --> 00:07:23.632
Oh, geez.

102
00:07:23.703 --> 00:07:26.005
Who is she?

103
00:07:26.077 --> 00:07:29.644
Okay, why are we on this case?
Just because Wilson asked?

104
00:07:29.721 --> 00:07:32.924
- Do I need a better reason?
- Well, most people wouldn't. You do.

105
00:07:44.631 --> 00:07:48.164
The only thing
we know for sure aboutJane Doe
is that her name isn'tJane Doe,

106
00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.972
which means no medical history.

107
00:07:50.046 --> 00:07:52.986
Allergies, medication,
previous diagnoses, treatment-

108
00:07:53.055 --> 00:07:56.462
We have no baseline,
no context for medical treatment.

109
00:07:56.531 --> 00:07:58.730
Wow.
Looks just like insulin.

110
00:08:00.142 --> 00:08:02.580
Vomit. Still moist.
[Sniffs]

111
00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:06.216
- What do you think? Couple of days old?
- Ugh! You trying to make me hurl?

112
00:08:06.292 --> 00:08:08.890
Yeah.
And here's the big finish.

113
00:08:10.271 --> 00:08:12.436
[Groans]
Salty.

114
00:08:12.511 --> 00:08:14.983
Chemical imbalance.

115
00:08:15.052 --> 00:08:17.456
Low magnesium
could cause a twitch.
Or high calcium.

116
00:08:17.526 --> 00:08:21.800
- Or it's a coincidence.
The point is, we don't know anything.
- So do the M.R.I. Find out.

117
00:08:21.871 --> 00:08:23.671
The M.R.I. Can wait.
Hang a banana bag.

118
00:08:23.743 --> 00:08:26.740
Give her 24 hours
to correct the electrolyte imbalance.
We'll take it from there.

119
00:08:26.819 --> 00:08:29.087
Great. Thanks.

120
00:08:35.076 --> 00:08:38.449
Okay, even if she's not faking,
what's so fascinating about this case?

121
00:08:38.519 --> 00:08:42.257
At the moment,
how much you don't want me to take it.

122
00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.324
That's pretty fascinating.

123
00:08:49.049 --> 00:08:50.986
[Chase]
Nice likeness of Dr. Foreman.

124
00:08:51.055 --> 00:08:54.519
In fact, he's never looked better.

125
00:08:55.836 --> 00:08:59.300
He doesn't like me.
I can tell.

126
00:08:59.379 --> 00:09:02.148
It's okay.
He doesn't like me either.

127
00:09:02.221 --> 00:09:05.458
- Who's James?
- [Groaning]

128
00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:08.937
Ow.!
Pain in your head?

129
00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:11.411
[Groans]
Get away from me!

130
00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.386
- No, no, no, no!
- All right, let's cool her out.
One milligram Ativan, push.

131
00:09:14.456 --> 00:09:16.724
No!
No, no, no, no, no, no!

132
00:09:16.796 --> 00:09:18.733
Hold on.

133
00:09:18.802 --> 00:09:20.670
[Grunting]
Aah! Aah!

134
00:09:20.741 --> 00:09:24.342
- [Screaming, Gasping]
- She bit me!

135
00:09:24.418 --> 00:09:28.589
- [Whimpering]
- Good news is, she's negative
for HIV and Hep "C."

136
00:09:28.664 --> 00:09:31.695
Yeah?
I'm getting a tetanus shot.
She's getting an M.R.I.

137
00:09:31.772 --> 00:09:35.270
- There's a two-day wait
for nonemergency M.R.I.'s.
- She's getting an M.R.I.! Then she's outta here.

138
00:09:37.021 --> 00:09:40.964
But Dr. Terhark specifically said
I'd have the M.R.I. At 10:00.

139
00:09:41.033 --> 00:09:44.634
It's almost 11:00,
and I haven't even had the pre-test yet.

140
00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:47.650
[Nurse]
Sorry. We're a little backed up.
[Exasperated Sigh]

141
00:09:47.718 --> 00:09:50.156
Excuse me.
You're Dr. Terhark's 10:00?

142
00:09:50.225 --> 00:09:54.168
I'm Angela Whitney.
I'm meeting my decorator at 11:30.

143
00:09:54.237 --> 00:09:56.675
She's coming all the way
from New York.

144
00:09:56.744 --> 00:09:59.182
Dr. Terhark promised
I'd be home in time.

145
00:09:59.251 --> 00:10:01.245
Of course.

146
00:10:12.723 --> 00:10:16.290
She just about prepped
for her M.R.I.?

147
00:10:16.367 --> 00:10:19.068
Mrs. Whitney?
[Beeping]

148
00:10:20.679 --> 00:10:23.916
You tried to steal
someone else's test.

149
00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.927
Dr. Terhark
is a plastic surgeon.

150
00:10:25.995 --> 00:10:29.596
The woman was
getting a six-month checkup
on her chin implants.

151
00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.348
- I can't believe you authorized this.
- Really?

152
00:10:33.416 --> 00:10:36.481
It sounds exactly
like something I'd do.

153
00:10:36.559 --> 00:10:38.189
She can't have an M.R.I.

154
00:10:39.568 --> 00:10:42.805
The C.T. Scan shows
she has a surgical pin in her arm.

155
00:10:42.877 --> 00:10:46.718
The M.R.I. Magnet
would have ripped it out ofher body.

156
00:10:46.789 --> 00:10:49.057
You like the Alien movies?

157
00:10:49.128 --> 00:10:52.296
You had no medical history.
What were you thinking?

158
00:10:52.371 --> 00:10:55.676
We'll surgically remove the pin,
then do the M.R.I.
Does that sound good?

159
00:10:56.617 --> 00:10:58.588
She has an electrolyte imbalance.

160
00:10:58.656 --> 00:11:01.687
Dr. Foreman, a neurologist,
believes this woman
has a brain tumor.

161
00:11:01.765 --> 00:11:05.036
- Actually, l-
- Hey, don't ever apologize
for a medical opinion.

162
00:11:05.108 --> 00:11:08.139
If he's right
and we don't do this test,
the patient dies.

163
00:11:08.217 --> 00:11:12.251
I realize that you have a specialty
of your own, but does yours have
anything to do with the brain?

164
00:11:12.329 --> 00:11:15.132
His does.

165
00:11:15.203 --> 00:11:17.140
Fine.

166
00:11:17.209 --> 00:11:20.912
- But nothing more
until you find out who she is.
- How are we supposed to-

167
00:11:20.987 --> 00:11:23.984
Hey! He knows
more homeless people
than any of us.

168
00:11:26.336 --> 00:11:29.174
Go check out the hood, dog.

169
00:11:34.627 --> 00:11:36.895
I don't know.

170
00:11:36.966 --> 00:11:42.710
I've seen a lot of faces around here,
but I don't think I know her.

171
00:11:44.154 --> 00:11:46.148
Great.

172
00:11:47.162 --> 00:11:50.433
Say, I, uh, like that jacket.

173
00:11:50.505 --> 00:11:54.208
Yeah, uh,
it's all comin' to me now.

174
00:11:54.283 --> 00:11:56.721
I know where she keeps her stuff.

175
00:12:01.537 --> 00:12:03.771
[Yells]
[Squeaking]

176
00:12:03.844 --> 00:12:05.838
Just bats.

177
00:12:06.952 --> 00:12:09.949
I thought the lining
would be thicker.

178
00:12:29.751 --> 00:12:32.189
No tumor. Nothing.
Her brain is clear.

179
00:12:32.259 --> 00:12:35.530
Which means that girl had surgery
just so you wouldn't get reamed out by Cuddy.

180
00:12:35.601 --> 00:12:38.838
Not necessarily.
There could still be something
neurological going on.

181
00:12:38.912 --> 00:12:41.111
Sure. She's not conning us.
The M.R.I. Is.

182
00:12:41.185 --> 00:12:45.253
Not wearing a coat in this weather.
That is so wrong.
She drew these.

183
00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.666
They might give us a clue.

184
00:12:47.736 --> 00:12:50.676
She sign them?
Her name would be a start.

185
00:12:50.745 --> 00:12:54.243
All the mythology, the locations,
they'd all depend on her life experience.

186
00:12:54.323 --> 00:12:56.488
Philadelphia.

187
00:12:56.562 --> 00:12:58.556
Look at that skyline.

188
00:12:58.635 --> 00:13:00.265
It's very evocative.

189
00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.106
The Chrysler Building.

190
00:13:02.178 --> 00:13:04.742
- That's a cloud.
- And the Chrysler Building's in New York.

191
00:13:04.819 --> 00:13:06.756
Ehh, I'm getting Philly.

192
00:13:06.825 --> 00:13:09.663
And that cactus,
well, it's a- it's a smashed car.

193
00:13:09.734 --> 00:13:13.335
- It's a car accident.
- A cactus in Philadelphia?

194
00:13:13.411 --> 00:13:16.476
Water.
Well, water's October, right?
Obviously.

195
00:13:16.552 --> 00:13:21.327
Well, the page number 22,
so that's October 2, 2002.

196
00:13:21.401 --> 00:13:24.432
Ergo, the patient was in a car accident
two years ago last October.

197
00:13:24.509 --> 00:13:27.141
My goodness.
Was she okay?

198
00:13:27.217 --> 00:13:29.154
Broke her arm, I think.

199
00:13:29.222 --> 00:13:31.991
They fixed it with this.

200
00:13:33.401 --> 00:13:35.669
Surgical pin.

201
00:13:35.742 --> 00:13:40.050
Better than a wallet.
Serial numbers in case of recall,
tied to a patient's name.

202
00:13:40.121 --> 00:13:44.589
That's why you insisted on the M.R.I. -
so you could remove
the surgical pin from her arm?

203
00:13:44.667 --> 00:13:48.165
- You didn't think I was gonna do it
to save your sorry ass, did you?
- [Fax Beeping, Printing]

204
00:13:48.244 --> 00:13:50.375
You might wanna
take a look at that.

205
00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.390
Her name is Victoria Matsen,
or at least that's the one she used then.

206
00:13:53.459 --> 00:13:56.558
Any hospital
with a record of treating her
should be sending that information.

207
00:13:56.635 --> 00:13:58.572
Oh, crap!

208
00:13:58.641 --> 00:14:01.581
Her blood work came back an hour ago.
Magnesium was normal.

209
00:14:01.649 --> 00:14:05.216
Did you change her banana bag?
Stopped the magnesium,
started iron dextran for severe anemia.

210
00:14:05.293 --> 00:14:07.230
She's allergic to iron dextran.

211
00:14:07.299 --> 00:14:09.669
[Monitor Alarms Beeping]
[Gasping, Wheezing]

212
00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:13.113
Grab some epi off the code cart.

213
00:14:13.183 --> 00:14:15.747
[Wheezing Continues]

214
00:14:15.824 --> 00:14:18.023
Respiratory arrest.
Call a code!

215
00:14:18.097 --> 00:14:20.832
- You're having an allergic reaction.
Can you speak?
- [Wheezing Continues]

216
00:14:20.905 --> 00:14:23.036
She's not getting any air.

217
00:14:23.112 --> 00:14:25.710
Got the epi.

218
00:14:25.786 --> 00:14:29.284
- Sats are down in the 80s and dropping.
- We have about another minute.

219
00:14:42.233 --> 00:14:44.671
[Foreman]
Well, we got her sedated
and stabilized.

220
00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:49.378
And you still think
there's nothing wrong with her?
Nothing's changed.

221
00:14:49.453 --> 00:14:51.687
You almost killed her.
That's different.

222
00:14:51.761 --> 00:14:54.393
And we know who she is.

223
00:14:54.468 --> 00:14:57.533
So far, we've heard from three hospitals
with records on Victoria Matsen.

224
00:14:57.611 --> 00:14:59.776
Seven visits going back two years.

225
00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:02.790
- [Wilson] Any home addresses?
- The pin in her arm
went in during an E.R. Visit.

226
00:15:02.859 --> 00:15:05.594
She wasn't conscious,
so they didn't get an address.

227
00:15:05.667 --> 00:15:08.573
- The other visits, she gave fake addresses.
- Any treatment for neurological problems?

228
00:15:08.642 --> 00:15:10.579
Anything that
might explain the twitch?

229
00:15:10.648 --> 00:15:13.816
Last winter,
Jefferson Hospital in Philly.
Got treated for frostbite.

230
00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:15.918
Baby, it's cold outside.

231
00:15:15.997 --> 00:15:18.766
And depression.
They put her on Prozac.

232
00:15:18.839 --> 00:15:21.779
Well, I'd be bummed out too.
Zero degrees, living in a box.

233
00:15:21.847 --> 00:15:24.616
Put her back on it.
She cheers up,
she might stop biting people.

234
00:15:24.689 --> 00:15:29.430
There's a billing record
from Hartman Hospital last year.
Two appointments, ultrasounds.

235
00:15:29.503 --> 00:15:31.668
Doesn't say what for.
Pregnant?

236
00:15:31.742 --> 00:15:34.010
Well, only if she was
expecting an elephant.

237
00:15:34.082 --> 00:15:36.281
Appointments
were ten months apart.

238
00:15:36.356 --> 00:15:39.296
Kept the first, blew off the second.

239
00:15:39.364 --> 00:15:41.198
Abdominal pain.

240
00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.538
- Her chart doesn't say-
- Wait a minute.

241
00:15:43.609 --> 00:15:46.047
She goes in the first time.

242
00:15:46.117 --> 00:15:49.752
They look, they can't find anything.
Ten months later, why should she
subject herself to that again?

243
00:15:49.828 --> 00:15:52.198
Why make a second appointment?
She didn't.

244
00:15:52.268 --> 00:15:54.364
The nurse made the appointment.

245
00:15:56.046 --> 00:16:00.080
They were looking-
They were looking for ovarian cancer.

246
00:16:00.157 --> 00:16:01.683
[Snickers]

247
00:16:01.762 --> 00:16:04.759
You got all of that
from one canceled appointment?

248
00:16:04.837 --> 00:16:07.435
With Jerry Lauseng, yeah.
He's an oncologist.

249
00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:12.147
Hang on. Her current blood work
doesn't show cancer.
C.A. 125 is normal.

250
00:16:12.225 --> 00:16:16.396
And the cancer wouldn't account
for the alleged twitch
or any ofher other alleged symptoms.

251
00:16:16.471 --> 00:16:18.237
Actually, it would.

252
00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:21.250
Neoplastic syndrome
associated with the cancer...

253
00:16:21.318 --> 00:16:24.953
could cause her
to twitch like a bunny
on crystal meth.

254
00:16:25.029 --> 00:16:27.023
Ultrasound her ovaries.

255
00:16:28.606 --> 00:16:33.552
- Did you find a brain tumor on her M.R.I.?
- No. Foreman was wrong.

256
00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:37.062
I'm starting to wonder about
that guy's medical chops.
Right.

257
00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:39.534
- Shelley Diamond.
- Yeah.

258
00:16:39.605 --> 00:16:42.169
Dr. House
is ready to see you now.

259
00:16:42.246 --> 00:16:46.520
The little ones are licking each other again,
and Harry's got a seeping wart
on his extra toe.

260
00:16:46.591 --> 00:16:48.528
What room should we go to?

261
00:16:48.597 --> 00:16:50.693
- [Sneezes]
- [Baby Laughs]

262
00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:54.234
[Groans]
You know what? I think I might be
coming down with something.

263
00:16:54.313 --> 00:16:56.911
Hate to give it to you guys.
Sorry.

264
00:16:56.987 --> 00:16:59.927
Oh, yeah. Just walk out.
Like I'm not gonna do anything.

265
00:16:59.996 --> 00:17:01.990
Bye-bye.

266
00:17:09.424 --> 00:17:11.658
Working hard?

267
00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:14.670
This stuff's pretty good.

268
00:17:14.739 --> 00:17:17.679
Calendraica works
for the Council of Genius.

269
00:17:17.747 --> 00:17:19.684
Bad guy is Mr. Fury.

270
00:17:19.753 --> 00:17:23.354
Fairly generic, no special skills,
but apparently very well organized.

271
00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:26.701
You think you work hard.
Try ruling the universe.

272
00:17:26.773 --> 00:17:29.007
You trying to teach me
something here?

273
00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:34.322
We got the flowing dress, the ring.
Think the patient was married?

274
00:17:34.396 --> 00:17:37.393
Maybe it was a bad break-up.
Maybe he dumped her
'cause she was on drugs.

275
00:17:38.741 --> 00:17:41.544
You care about her personal history?
No.

276
00:17:41.616 --> 00:17:44.180
Question is, why don't you?

277
00:17:45.461 --> 00:17:48.766
I hate to cite a cliche,
but Dad on the streets?

278
00:17:50.776 --> 00:17:53.248
- Dad's with Mom.
- They're both living on the streets?

279
00:17:53.316 --> 00:17:55.686
No. On a pension.

280
00:17:56.760 --> 00:18:00.395
- So, who pissed you off?
- [Scoffs]

281
00:18:00.471 --> 00:18:02.465
Right now, you.

282
00:18:08.327 --> 00:18:11.267
[House] Your turn.
You gonna tell me why this case?

283
00:18:11.335 --> 00:18:13.773
She's my new girlfriend.
I'm having a tattoo designed.

284
00:18:13.842 --> 00:18:16.280
I was hoping
you could find out her name.

285
00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:21.296
So she's just another sick person
that kindly Dr. Wilson has made sure
doesn't get lost in the big, ugly system.

286
00:18:21.364 --> 00:18:24.304
Yes, I forgot.
I need a reason to give a crap.

287
00:18:24.373 --> 00:18:27.313
You're giving two craps.
The metric system
always confuses me.

288
00:18:27.382 --> 00:18:29.285
Dr. House?

289
00:18:30.356 --> 00:18:34.664
- Time for Girl Scout cookies already?
- Get me some thin mints.

290
00:18:34.735 --> 00:18:37.903
Since you're too sick
to work in the clinic-

291
00:18:39.048 --> 00:18:41.418
[Exhales]
Okay.

292
00:18:41.488 --> 00:18:43.892
- I thought you-
- [Sneezes]

293
00:18:46.069 --> 00:18:49.476
I thought
you could do some teaching.
Patient histories.

294
00:18:49.545 --> 00:18:51.744
My specialty.

295
00:18:51.819 --> 00:18:54.223
When you teach,
you learn so much.
Don't you think?

296
00:18:54.292 --> 00:18:56.787
It's all about the giving back.

297
00:18:59.474 --> 00:19:03.007
Good old Cuddy.
Always thinking.

298
00:19:03.084 --> 00:19:05.454
She assign you
a patient to interview?

299
00:19:05.524 --> 00:19:07.256
Mm-hmm.
Mm-hmm.

300
00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.825
Then why are you still here?

301
00:19:18.094 --> 00:19:22.162
[Chase] Why are we on this case?
'Cause Wilson asked House
to do him a favor.

302
00:19:22.239 --> 00:19:25.612
I think House just wants to prove she's sick
so Foreman will be wrong.

303
00:19:25.682 --> 00:19:28.850
- Oh, you boys.
- Hey, I'm just doing my job.

304
00:19:30.529 --> 00:19:32.557
Whoa.

305
00:19:34.073 --> 00:19:39.487
Foreman's gonna be so embarrassed
when he finds out she's got cancer.

306
00:19:45.139 --> 00:19:48.512
Ah. I thought you were
too sick to be down here.

307
00:19:48.581 --> 00:19:52.045
I had to get away from those students,
so I faked a page.

308
00:19:52.125 --> 00:19:56.763
Foreman's parents,
happily married, 40 years.

309
00:19:56.839 --> 00:19:58.901
Mazel tov.
Kein ayin hara.

310
00:19:58.978 --> 00:20:02.420
So why does he hate
homeless people?

311
00:20:02.489 --> 00:20:07.903
I mean, if it's an uncle or a grandparent,
you'd think he'd use it
in his college application essay.

312
00:20:07.971 --> 00:20:11.276
Family struggles
beats a 4.0 G.P.A. Any day.

313
00:20:11.347 --> 00:20:15.951
- I think he had a 4.0.
- Maybe he's just a snob.

314
00:20:16.027 --> 00:20:18.967
You really don't need to know
everything about everybody.

315
00:20:19.036 --> 00:20:21.976
I don't need to watch The O.C.,
but it makes me happy.

316
00:20:22.044 --> 00:20:24.516
Yeah, delirious.
What's the other file?

317
00:20:26.791 --> 00:20:29.959
Wilson, James.
Boy Wonder Oncologist.

318
00:20:30.034 --> 00:20:31.868
You know him?

319
00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:36.715
You know, in some cultures,
it's considered almost rude
for one friend to spy on another.

320
00:20:36.787 --> 00:20:42.201
Of course, in Swedish,
the word "friend" can also be
translated as "limping twerp."

321
00:20:42.269 --> 00:20:44.833
[Pager Beeping]

322
00:20:46.816 --> 00:20:50.657
Did your pager really just go off,
or are you ditching the conversation?

323
00:20:50.727 --> 00:20:53.256
Why can't both be true?
Come on.

324
00:20:55.274 --> 00:20:57.838
Solid, noncystic mass
on the left ovary.

325
00:20:57.915 --> 00:20:59.909
Five-by-three centimeters.

326
00:20:59.988 --> 00:21:01.925
Central necrosis.

327
00:21:01.994 --> 00:21:05.960
The only question is whether
she dies in two months or three.

328
00:21:06.038 --> 00:21:07.975
God.
You were right.

329
00:21:08.044 --> 00:21:11.782
There's nothing we can do for her here.
Might as well put her back on the street.

330
00:21:13.025 --> 00:21:14.791
Unless it's not cancer.

331
00:21:14.864 --> 00:21:17.633
- Ah, you're joking.
- Well, hard not to.

332
00:21:17.705 --> 00:21:19.699
Nothing funnier than cancer.

333
00:21:21.282 --> 00:21:25.556
What if it's a tuberculoma?
She's living out on the streets,
breathing all kinds of crap 24-7.

334
00:21:25.628 --> 00:21:28.500
The odds are, she's got T.B.
Why can't she have
a nice, benign growth to go with it?

335
00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:32.513
A solid mass on her ovary.
Ovarian cancer's way more likely.

336
00:21:34.086 --> 00:21:36.958
You're right.
It's not even close.

337
00:21:37.027 --> 00:21:39.431
Start her on I.N.H.,
rifampin and streptomycin.

338
00:21:39.501 --> 00:21:42.065
But that's the treatment
for a tuberculoma.

339
00:21:42.142 --> 00:21:45.880
And what is the treatment
for advanced ovarian cancer?

340
00:21:48.126 --> 00:21:49.721
Pine box.

341
00:21:55.915 --> 00:22:00.257
[Man On P.A.]
Oncologist to Nuclear Medicine.
Oncologist to Nuclear Medicine.

342
00:22:00.327 --> 00:22:03.734
What are you giving me?
A second dose
of antibiotics.

343
00:22:03.805 --> 00:22:08.307
If you've got a tuberculoma,
it should help.

344
00:22:09.387 --> 00:22:11.791
I don't have a tuberculoma, do I?

345
00:22:15.472 --> 00:22:18.675
[Sighs]
Probably not.

346
00:22:23.227 --> 00:22:26.360
Hey, listen.
I'm sorry I didn't believe you.

347
00:22:28.375 --> 00:22:30.471
I'm sorry I lied to you.

348
00:22:30.548 --> 00:22:33.647
I took too much insulin on purpose.

349
00:22:33.724 --> 00:22:36.721
I really wanted a place to sleep.

350
00:22:44.756 --> 00:22:47.855
Were you ever married, Victoria?

351
00:22:49.469 --> 00:22:52.672
But in the comic, it-
Well, it's a comic.
Comics are just made up.

352
00:22:54.216 --> 00:22:56.917
So who's James?

353
00:22:56.991 --> 00:23:00.433
Is he real, or did you make him up?

354
00:23:02.406 --> 00:23:04.742
He's real.

355
00:23:04.814 --> 00:23:07.879
Can I help you find him?

356
00:23:11.332 --> 00:23:15.332
Oh, the- the light's bright.

357
00:23:15.411 --> 00:23:18.510
It's getting brighter-
Oh- Ow.! Oh.!

358
00:23:18.587 --> 00:23:20.558
Hey, take it easy.
Everything's fine.

359
00:23:20.625 --> 00:23:24.363
Mr. Fury wants to hurt me!
Please help me!

360
00:23:24.437 --> 00:23:26.705
Doctor!
Wait, wait, wait.

361
00:23:26.777 --> 00:23:29.375
Hold on, hold on.
Please turn off the light!

362
00:23:29.451 --> 00:23:31.946
Please! Oh, God!
[Gasping, Whimpering]

363
00:23:32.025 --> 00:23:34.965
All right, hold on, Victoria.

364
00:23:35.034 --> 00:23:37.336
Hold on. Take it easy.
Everything's fine.

365
00:23:37.407 --> 00:23:40.108
- It's burning!
- Everything's fine, Victoria.

366
00:23:40.182 --> 00:23:42.050
It's burning!
Hold on.

367
00:23:42.121 --> 00:23:45.254
I'm burning!
Take a sip, take a sip.

368
00:23:45.330 --> 00:23:48.669
[Gasps] It's poison!
You gave me poison!

369
00:23:48.740 --> 00:23:50.677
Hold on.

370
00:23:50.746 --> 00:23:53.549
[Gasping, Screaming]
Take it easy.

371
00:23:54.958 --> 00:23:57.453
- [Screaming Continues]
- Hey, turn off that damn light!

372
00:23:57.532 --> 00:23:59.663
Help me, please.!

373
00:23:59.738 --> 00:24:05.152
Take it easy. Take it easy.
The bad guys can't get you here.
I've got you covered.

374
00:24:05.220 --> 00:24:07.955
But Mr. Fury's not the bad guy.

375
00:24:08.029 --> 00:24:11.026
I'm the bad guy.
It's me. I'm the bad guy.

376
00:24:11.104 --> 00:24:13.576
[Crying]

377
00:24:17.289 --> 00:24:19.226
It's not a tuberculoma.

378
00:24:19.295 --> 00:24:21.061
Can't be.

379
00:24:21.133 --> 00:24:25.544
I didn't know the biopsy
was back.
Her temperature's 105.

380
00:24:26.515 --> 00:24:28.611
The treatment's not working.
It's cancer.

381
00:24:28.689 --> 00:24:30.683
She's dying.

382
00:24:31.697 --> 00:24:34.398
105.
[Chase]
Good news.

383
00:24:34.471 --> 00:24:38.574
It's a tuberculoma.
How do you figure that?
Her temp's through the roof.

384
00:24:38.650 --> 00:24:42.684
The lab results from the biopsy.
It's definitely a tuberculoma.

385
00:24:46.105 --> 00:24:49.376
So, we're right about the diagnosis,

386
00:24:49.448 --> 00:24:52.981
and the treatment for that diagnosis
is killing her.

387
00:24:55.265 --> 00:24:57.396
Perfect.

388
00:24:57.471 --> 00:25:00.411
[Chase]
The lab checked the biopsy
again, twice.

389
00:25:00.479 --> 00:25:03.419
Well, a tuberculoma doesn't
give you a temperature of 105.

390
00:25:03.488 --> 00:25:05.516
Then it's a tuberculoma
and something else.

391
00:25:05.594 --> 00:25:08.762
The "something else"
is gonna melt her brain.
Poach.

392
00:25:09.640 --> 00:25:11.668
Better metaphor.

393
00:25:11.746 --> 00:25:15.119
A fever that high
has to be bacterial.

394
00:25:15.189 --> 00:25:19.030
- Maybe the bowel got nicked in the biopsy.
- I did the biopsy. No nick.

395
00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:22.598
- She could have picked up
an infection on the streets.
- She didn't have a fever when I admitted her.

396
00:25:22.677 --> 00:25:26.620
The Prozac we gave her could have
triggered serotonin syndrome,
which would explain the fever.

397
00:25:26.689 --> 00:25:29.390
- No. Jefferson put her on Prozac
and it wasn't a problem.
- She probably never took it!

398
00:25:29.463 --> 00:25:32.768
Most likely, they saw her one time
and dumped her out of the E.R.
With a scrip.

399
00:25:32.839 --> 00:25:37.409
- Oh, just like you were gonna do!
- Okay, you two. Grab some scalpels
and settle this like doctors.

400
00:25:39.392 --> 00:25:41.420
Send blood and urine cultures
and get a chest X-ray.

401
00:25:41.498 --> 00:25:45.601
Fine, take her off the Prozac
and put her on Bromocryptene
for the serotonin syndrome.

402
00:25:45.676 --> 00:25:50.383
Might wanna get her in an ice bath as well,
assuming we want her to live long enough
to see those test results.

403
00:25:55.037 --> 00:25:57.031
I said I was sorry.

404
00:25:57.110 --> 00:26:01.076
Your fever's 105.
If we don't bring it down fast-

405
00:26:01.155 --> 00:26:03.217
Foreman,
why are you doing this to me?

406
00:26:03.294 --> 00:26:05.197
I'm saving your life.

407
00:26:05.266 --> 00:26:10.303
[Whimpering, Sobbing]
No, don't make me go in there, please.
Don't make me do it, please!

408
00:26:10.381 --> 00:26:12.945
I don't wanna go!

409
00:26:13.022 --> 00:26:14.788
Come on.
You can do this.

410
00:26:20.343 --> 00:26:23.283
[Whimpering Continues]

411
00:26:23.351 --> 00:26:26.348
[Screaming Continues]

412
00:26:34.685 --> 00:26:36.519
Please.!

413
00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:44.946
Seventeen-year-old female
presents with abrasions and
apparent trauma injury to her wrist.

414
00:26:45.014 --> 00:26:48.011
Dr. House?
Continue.

415
00:26:49.126 --> 00:26:51.063
You're reading a comic book.

416
00:26:51.132 --> 00:26:54.630
And you're calling attention to your bosom
by wearing a low-cut top.

417
00:26:55.979 --> 00:26:59.421
Oh, I'm sorry.
I thought we were having
a"state the obvious" contest.

418
00:26:59.489 --> 00:27:01.426
I'm competitive by nature.

419
00:27:01.495 --> 00:27:04.435
I thought you were
supposed to be listening to
our patient histories.

420
00:27:04.504 --> 00:27:08.949
No, I'm supposed to be teaching you.
If I can do that without listening,
more power to me.

421
00:27:09.016 --> 00:27:10.542
Seventeen-year-old female-

422
00:27:10.621 --> 00:27:15.727
If this guy's supposed to have
universal power over all gravity,
how come his hair won't stay down?

423
00:27:15.803 --> 00:27:17.740
That's just stupid.

424
00:27:17.809 --> 00:27:20.749
- She fell offher horse
while riding in the county fair.
- No, she didn't.

425
00:27:20.818 --> 00:27:25.320
She fell off the steps of her beach house.
You must have gone to the wrong room.

426
00:27:25.397 --> 00:27:30.138
Hard to believe that one patient
could slip past Cuddy and get herself
admitted with a sprained wrist.

427
00:27:30.211 --> 00:27:32.649
Two seems almost impossible.
What room?

428
00:27:32.718 --> 00:27:34.780
[Together]
Room 2106.

429
00:27:36.229 --> 00:27:39.362
Patients lie,
but usually only one lie at a time.

430
00:27:39.438 --> 00:27:41.375
How much does she weigh?

431
00:27:41.443 --> 00:27:44.440
- It's her wrist, not her weight-
- Poundage, ladies.

432
00:27:44.519 --> 00:27:47.824
- And by-the-by, what color's her nose?
- She's thin.

433
00:27:47.896 --> 00:27:50.460
- Flesh tone?
- What does this have to do
with her wrist?

434
00:27:50.536 --> 00:27:52.974
[Pager Beeping]
Almost nothing.

435
00:27:53.043 --> 00:27:57.420
She's either under ninety pounds
or she has a red nose. I gotta go.

436
00:27:57.490 --> 00:27:59.518
- What's wrong with her?
- [Sighs]

437
00:27:59.596 --> 00:28:02.399
That would be telling.

438
00:28:02.471 --> 00:28:05.274
Oh, I am just too nice.

439
00:28:06.415 --> 00:28:08.215
It starts with "C."

440
00:28:11.162 --> 00:28:14.227
- Urine cultures are negative.
- So is the chest X-ray.

441
00:28:14.304 --> 00:28:18.806
- I assume there's a positive coming.
- Lumbar punctures reveal
elevated proteins and white counts.

442
00:28:18.885 --> 00:28:21.323
C.S.F. Cultures?
Still brewing.

443
00:28:21.392 --> 00:28:24.491
Nothing on gram stain.
It looks like meningitis.

444
00:28:24.568 --> 00:28:27.907
[Chase]
We know it's definitely an infection,
and we know where it is.

445
00:28:27.977 --> 00:28:30.176
Well, meningitis
is nice and simple.

446
00:28:30.250 --> 00:28:33.190
Get her in isolation
and start her on Ceftriaxone.

447
00:28:33.259 --> 00:28:35.754
Either she gets better,
or she dies.

448
00:28:37.070 --> 00:28:39.565
Let me know which one happens.

449
00:28:46.331 --> 00:28:48.462
Oh, my God!
She was sedated.

450
00:28:48.537 --> 00:28:51.238
[Chase] It must have worn off.
[Foreman]
I did it myself a halfhour ago.

451
00:28:51.311 --> 00:28:53.305
I'll check
the nurse's station.

452
00:28:54.888 --> 00:28:56.882
Calendraica.

453
00:29:14.244 --> 00:29:16.238
She's gonna die out there.

454
00:29:18.891 --> 00:29:22.492
You don't walk out of a room
with 10 milligrams of Haldol
in your system.

455
00:29:22.568 --> 00:29:25.508
You don't walk at all.
It was 10 milligrams!
I gave it to her.

456
00:29:25.576 --> 00:29:29.018
It doesn't matter!
Bacterial meningitis-
highly contagious.

457
00:29:29.087 --> 00:29:32.426
If she is out of the hospital,
we are so liable.

458
00:29:32.496 --> 00:29:35.265
Not to worry. She'll be dead
before she can kill anybody.

459
00:29:35.338 --> 00:29:38.745
Security tape confirms it.
She stole some clothes
and she's gone.

460
00:29:38.814 --> 00:29:40.717
[Door Closes]

461
00:29:41.522 --> 00:29:45.590
Wrong coat.
The cape's in the closet.
I had it cleaned.

462
00:29:45.667 --> 00:29:48.766
- Funny.
- You gonna save her?

463
00:29:48.843 --> 00:29:51.783
[Sighs] In her comics,
Mr. Fury lives in Sloan Harbor.

464
00:29:51.852 --> 00:29:55.123
The night she came in,
she was at a rave at 1408 Sloan Street.

465
00:29:55.195 --> 00:29:58.033
You've been reading.
My, how you've changed.

466
00:29:58.104 --> 00:30:00.303
You are a doctor.
Do what doctors do.

467
00:30:00.377 --> 00:30:04.845
Pick up the phone, dial 911,
and a cop on the other end
does what cops do...

468
00:30:04.923 --> 00:30:07.487
and finds the missing person.

469
00:30:07.564 --> 00:30:11.405
I assume the rest of you
have doctor things to do.
I know you do.

470
00:30:13.047 --> 00:30:15.748
- Cacchi-Ricci Disease.
- Do you even know what that is?

471
00:30:15.821 --> 00:30:18.761
Or are you just guessing
everything that starts with "C"?

472
00:30:18.830 --> 00:30:22.397
The kidney problems
could result in weight loss.
Cacchi. C-A-C-

473
00:30:22.473 --> 00:30:24.410
Oh, geez,
she's going alphabetically.

474
00:30:24.479 --> 00:30:27.043
Doctor, why are you
wearing that bird pin?

475
00:30:28.090 --> 00:30:30.084
It sets off my eyes.

476
00:30:31.366 --> 00:30:34.238
Hi, Jodi. I'm Dr. House.
What brings you to the hospital?

477
00:30:34.308 --> 00:30:37.077
My wrist.
How did that happen?

478
00:30:37.149 --> 00:30:41.183
I was riding the Ferris wheel,
and this huge seagull flew right at me.

479
00:30:41.261 --> 00:30:43.129
How horrifying.

480
00:30:43.199 --> 00:30:46.139
I swung my arm at the bird,
but I hit the Ferris wheel.

481
00:30:48.348 --> 00:30:50.616
She's making it all up?

482
00:30:50.689 --> 00:30:53.788
- No, her wrist really does hurt.
- I'm not lying.

483
00:30:53.864 --> 00:30:57.967
Of course you are.
You have no idea what happened.
You have no memory.

484
00:31:02.054 --> 00:31:03.991
Korsakoff's syndrome.

485
00:31:04.060 --> 00:31:07.833
Her brain is damaged by
excessive drinking or insufficient diet,
pretty obviously the latter.

486
00:31:07.904 --> 00:31:10.673
She has no new memories,
no new ideas.

487
00:31:10.746 --> 00:31:12.683
Can't even process that idea.

488
00:31:12.752 --> 00:31:15.384
So her brain fills the gaps
as best it can using visual clues.

489
00:31:15.459 --> 00:31:18.399
The horse on your shirt
led her to the riding accident,

490
00:31:18.468 --> 00:31:21.169
and the surfscene
on your clipboard
led her to the beach.

491
00:31:21.243 --> 00:31:23.841
"Korsakoff"
doesn't start with a "C."

492
00:31:23.917 --> 00:31:26.355
I didn't say "C."

493
00:31:26.425 --> 00:31:28.362
Or did I?

494
00:31:28.431 --> 00:31:33.103
Lesson to be learned-
treat everybody as if they have Korsakoff's.
We all lie anyway.

495
00:31:33.178 --> 00:31:35.480
Give her thiamine right away.
She'll bounce back pretty quickly.

496
00:31:35.551 --> 00:31:38.423
And then get her to eat
some cake and ice cream.

497
00:31:38.493 --> 00:31:40.761
Yes?

498
00:31:40.833 --> 00:31:43.773
Did you need to be so cruel?
I think she's crying.

499
00:31:48.387 --> 00:31:52.330
Hi, Jodi. I'm Dr. House.
What happened to your wrist?

500
00:31:52.399 --> 00:31:54.598
There was this weird old guy.
He had a cane.

501
00:31:54.672 --> 00:31:56.871
See?
It's like it never happened.

502
00:31:56.945 --> 00:31:59.817
Perfect forgiveness.

503
00:32:03.465 --> 00:32:05.402
Pulse is rapid.
You got a temp?

504
00:32:05.470 --> 00:32:08.239
Don't know. She's warm, but-
Might be something to look into.
She has meningitis.

505
00:32:08.312 --> 00:32:11.218
Sorry. I was more worried
about her heart blowing up.
Pulse is 150.

506
00:32:11.287 --> 00:32:13.053
Rhythm regular?
Yeah.

507
00:32:13.126 --> 00:32:16.397
Ready?
One, two, three.

508
00:32:16.468 --> 00:32:19.032
- Where'd you find her?
- Battlefield State Park.

509
00:32:19.109 --> 00:32:20.704
She narrow complex?
Uh-huh.

510
00:32:20.781 --> 00:32:25.226
- She wasn't at Sloan?
- She was just passed out on the grass.

511
00:32:25.294 --> 00:32:28.097
Foreman.
I need Foreman.

512
00:32:28.837 --> 00:32:32.678
All right. Supraventricular tachycardia.
Get me adenosine, one milligram, I.V. Push.

513
00:32:32.749 --> 00:32:34.743
Right away.
Thank you.

514
00:32:42.310 --> 00:32:44.247
Hang in there.

515
00:32:48.560 --> 00:32:50.497
[Foreman]
Her arrhythmia's stabilized.

516
00:32:50.566 --> 00:32:55.672
Doesn't make sense.
What would push her heart rate
over 150? Dehydration?

517
00:32:55.748 --> 00:32:58.449
- Fever?
- Unlikely. By themselves,
neither one would do it.

518
00:32:58.523 --> 00:33:01.326
We must be wrong
about the meningitis.
Maybe it's structural heart disease.

519
00:33:01.398 --> 00:33:04.635
Her heart rate dropped
when you administered the adenosine.

520
00:33:04.708 --> 00:33:07.546
In two seconds.

521
00:33:07.615 --> 00:33:09.849
It's still meningitis.

522
00:33:09.923 --> 00:33:14.231
If it is, with the delay in treatment,
she's-she's got almost no chance.

523
00:33:14.302 --> 00:33:16.672
Start the treatment.

524
00:33:18.581 --> 00:33:21.521
Read the report.
I found her lying on the grass.

525
00:33:21.590 --> 00:33:25.533
You should read my reports.
I make up stuff all the time.

526
00:33:25.601 --> 00:33:28.199
What really happened?

527
00:33:28.275 --> 00:33:30.269
Well, since it's you-

528
00:33:32.320 --> 00:33:34.918
I found her lying on the grass.

529
00:33:38.137 --> 00:33:40.074
Wow.

530
00:33:40.143 --> 00:33:42.274
That is a great-looking gun.

531
00:33:42.349 --> 00:33:44.719
It's not a gun.
It's a Taser.

532
00:33:44.789 --> 00:33:47.261
It's so cool-looking.
What does it do?

533
00:33:47.330 --> 00:33:49.894
Fire about 60,000 volts?

534
00:33:49.971 --> 00:33:53.276
At least that's what it would take
to jack someone's heart up to 150.

535
00:33:53.347 --> 00:33:55.785
Okay, okay.

536
00:33:55.855 --> 00:34:00.824
Let's just say
I tell you what happened.
It stays between you and me. Right?

537
00:34:02.173 --> 00:34:05.546
I found her lying on the grass.

538
00:34:06.619 --> 00:34:08.351
Fine.

539
00:34:08.424 --> 00:34:11.022
Don't tell me.

540
00:34:11.099 --> 00:34:13.333
Tell my friend, Ben Franklin.

541
00:34:13.405 --> 00:34:18.751
[Woman On P.A.]
Dr. Wharton to the research lab.
Dr. Wharton to the research lab.

542
00:34:20.125 --> 00:34:23.430
I watch a lot of cop shows.

543
00:34:29.017 --> 00:34:32.459
The good news is, the heart rate thing
is not connected to her condition.

544
00:34:33.697 --> 00:34:37.902
Well, then she's dying, 'cause
the meningitis treatment isn't helping her.
She's getting worse.

545
00:34:39.246 --> 00:34:41.616
Well, that brings us
to the bad news.

546
00:34:41.686 --> 00:34:44.318
The cop Tasered her.

547
00:34:44.394 --> 00:34:48.428
[Scoffs] Jerk. Probably couldn't
get to his real gun fast enough.

548
00:34:48.506 --> 00:34:51.309
First time he hit her in the thigh...

549
00:34:51.382 --> 00:34:53.513
and shejust kept going,
like it was nothing.

550
00:34:53.588 --> 00:34:56.083
Right about here.

551
00:35:11.873 --> 00:35:13.867
She didn't feel the Taser.

552
00:35:20.933 --> 00:35:24.204
Localized numbness?
Yeah, in that one spot.

553
00:35:24.276 --> 00:35:26.372
The diabetes?

554
00:35:26.449 --> 00:35:28.614
I don't think so.

555
00:35:29.892 --> 00:35:33.630
Well, no alcohol.
Not entrapment syndrome.

556
00:35:33.703 --> 00:35:36.541
Can't be a vitamin deficiency.

557
00:35:36.612 --> 00:35:39.609
We can't chase down
every sensory neuropathy.

558
00:35:43.832 --> 00:35:46.704
Is that where she bit you?
Yeah.

559
00:35:53.059 --> 00:35:54.654
What the hell!

560
00:35:56.034 --> 00:35:58.974
Can't get angry
if you don't feel anything.

561
00:36:04.291 --> 00:36:06.695
First, there's localized numbness,

562
00:36:08.169 --> 00:36:10.904
then sensitivity to light,

563
00:36:10.977 --> 00:36:13.347
disorientation, paranoia,

564
00:36:13.417 --> 00:36:17.086
ineffectiveness of sedatives,
and then hydrophobia.

565
00:36:18.566 --> 00:36:20.560
Fear of water.

566
00:36:21.875 --> 00:36:24.313
Rabies.

567
00:36:24.383 --> 00:36:28.326
There have only been, what,
10 cases in the last 20 years?

568
00:36:28.394 --> 00:36:32.428
Yeah, that's because nonhomeless people,
when they get bitten, they get shots.

569
00:36:32.506 --> 00:36:34.101
There were bats.

570
00:36:35.815 --> 00:36:37.809
[Beeping]

571
00:36:48.352 --> 00:36:50.790
She's dying.

572
00:36:52.864 --> 00:36:55.336
There's no treatment.

573
00:36:56.843 --> 00:36:59.407
How much time does she have?

574
00:36:59.484 --> 00:37:01.421
A day. Maybe two.

575
00:37:01.490 --> 00:37:05.193
And if you don't get your shot
in the next, say, three hours,

576
00:37:05.267 --> 00:37:08.538
I'm gonna have to make
another affirmative action hire.

577
00:37:10.883 --> 00:37:12.877
Come on.

578
00:37:19.274 --> 00:37:21.040
[Foreman Sighs]
Do it.

579
00:37:23.821 --> 00:37:25.986
[Groans]

580
00:37:26.060 --> 00:37:28.727
You want me to talk to her?

581
00:37:28.801 --> 00:37:31.536
And say what?

582
00:37:31.609 --> 00:37:36.783
"There's some experimental treatment
that's not gonna work"? No.

583
00:37:38.061 --> 00:37:40.533
"But don't worry,
we can make you comfortable"?

584
00:37:40.602 --> 00:37:44.009
[Winces]
Doesn't matter.

585
00:37:44.079 --> 00:37:47.817
Now she's gonna die in that room.

586
00:37:47.890 --> 00:37:49.827
Yeah.

587
00:37:49.896 --> 00:37:51.833
That's what you say to her.

588
00:37:51.901 --> 00:37:54.739
Keep that there
and rest for a minute.

589
00:37:56.214 --> 00:37:58.550
[Groans]
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

590
00:37:58.620 --> 00:38:01.184
Tell House I need to go out
for about an hour.

591
00:38:01.261 --> 00:38:03.928
She may not have that long.

592
00:38:08.348 --> 00:38:10.342
I don't want her to die alone.

593
00:38:11.725 --> 00:38:13.719
You're going to find James.

594
00:38:13.798 --> 00:38:15.860
I'm gonna try.

595
00:38:26.100 --> 00:38:30.271
Well, I must say,
he's done a lot with the place.

596
00:38:37.632 --> 00:38:39.626
Hello?

597
00:39:00.766 --> 00:39:02.703
Hey.

598
00:39:02.772 --> 00:39:04.504
This is it.

599
00:39:10.160 --> 00:39:13.829
Man. No one's been in here
for a long time.

600
00:39:27.209 --> 00:39:29.203
It's gotta beJames.

601
00:39:30.618 --> 00:39:32.612
Maybe there's another address.

602
00:39:34.630 --> 00:39:36.624
That's notJames.

603
00:39:40.112 --> 00:39:41.912
Paul.

604
00:39:41.985 --> 00:39:43.888
Paul Furia.

605
00:39:45.060 --> 00:39:46.655
Mr. Fury.

606
00:39:46.732 --> 00:39:50.003
Her husband.

607
00:39:50.075 --> 00:39:52.673
Then who's James?

608
00:39:58.499 --> 00:40:00.493
Her kid.

609
00:40:11.469 --> 00:40:14.409
[Victoria]
Aw, I just wanna eat you up.
You're so delicious.!

610
00:40:14.478 --> 00:40:16.415
[Kissing]

611
00:40:16.484 --> 00:40:18.421
Aw, look at me.

612
00:40:18.489 --> 00:40:22.432
You're just like your papa.
Look at you! Just like your dad.

613
00:40:23.571 --> 00:40:25.337
Foreman.

614
00:40:25.409 --> 00:40:27.677
Foreman?

615
00:40:27.750 --> 00:40:29.448
[Sighs]

616
00:40:30.758 --> 00:40:32.752
They're dead.

617
00:40:35.238 --> 00:40:38.611
That car crash two years ago-

618
00:40:40.119 --> 00:40:44.153
She broke her arm,
and they were killed.

619
00:40:47.306 --> 00:40:49.540
She was driving.

620
00:41:15.488 --> 00:41:17.790
James.

621
00:41:17.861 --> 00:41:20.231
No.

622
00:41:20.301 --> 00:41:23.606
It's Paul.
Paul?

623
00:41:25.382 --> 00:41:27.718
You've come to take me.

624
00:41:28.859 --> 00:41:30.853
No.

625
00:41:32.035 --> 00:41:34.029
I've come to forgive you.

626
00:41:34.108 --> 00:41:36.444
[Gasps]

627
00:41:39.022 --> 00:41:40.959
It wasn't your fault.

628
00:41:41.028 --> 00:41:43.466
[Sobbing]

629
00:41:45.640 --> 00:41:48.238
I'm so sorry.

630
00:41:48.315 --> 00:41:51.414
I'm so sorry.
I'm so sorry.

631
00:41:53.028 --> 00:41:55.729
I know.
[Sobbing Continues]

632
00:41:55.803 --> 00:41:58.709
It's okay, Victoria.

633
00:41:58.778 --> 00:42:00.772
It's okay.

634
00:42:00.851 --> 00:42:03.346
[Gasping, Sobbing]

635
00:42:12.886 --> 00:42:14.880
[Sighs]

636
00:42:17.065 --> 00:42:19.503
Oh.

637
00:42:19.571 --> 00:42:21.565
You followed me?

638
00:42:22.915 --> 00:42:24.852
No.

639
00:42:24.920 --> 00:42:29.023
You were wearing rain boots today,
but you were parked
in the underground garage,

640
00:42:29.099 --> 00:42:34.171
so the only reason you'd need boots
was if you were hitting the streets.

641
00:42:34.247 --> 00:42:36.446
I followed you.

642
00:42:36.520 --> 00:42:39.893
Didn't we have a conversation
about friendship?
Yeah.

643
00:42:39.964 --> 00:42:42.733
I had some follow-up questions.

644
00:42:44.778 --> 00:42:47.809
I've met your parents
and your brother.

645
00:42:47.887 --> 00:42:50.257
I have two brothers.

646
00:42:52.768 --> 00:42:56.039
Why wouldn't you tell me-
It wasn't relevant.

647
00:42:56.110 --> 00:42:59.449
Why not?
Because he's not
in my life anymore.

648
00:43:00.791 --> 00:43:02.785
Well, that's relevant.

649
00:43:07.142 --> 00:43:10.241
This was the last place I saw him.

650
00:43:10.318 --> 00:43:12.483
Nine years ago.

651
00:43:15.500 --> 00:43:19.443
I don't even know if he's alive.

652
00:44:10.291 --> 00:44:11.555
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>

